--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e9620f8c34305754d8cc9a7e49e852d9, type: 3}
  m_Name: SpaceExplorerTexts_en
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_LocaleId:
    m_Code: en
  m_SharedData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 6c9825274246e407d8d990969f77224e, type: 2}
  m_Metadata:
    m_Items: []
  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 72623316992
    m_Localized: Space Explorer
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 13577434947584
    m_Localized: Earth
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 13727754608640
    m_Localized: Jupiter
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 13822084505600
    m_Localized: Mars
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 13860193951744
    m_Localized: Mercury
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 13878153961472
    m_Localized: Neptune
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 13902636113920
    m_Localized: Saturn
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 13929035063296
    m_Localized: Uranus
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 13950480539648
    m_Localized: Venus
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 26792768299008
    m_Localized: Space Lab
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 29384084807680
    m_Localized: "Earth is the only planet we know that has life \u2014 that means
      plants, animals, and people all live here!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 29610447200256
    m_Localized: "About 70% of Earth is covered in water, which is why it's sometimes
      called the \u201CBlue Planet.\u201D"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 29627203444736
    m_Localized: "Earth has air we can breathe, made mostly of nitrogen and oxygen
      \u2014 super important for all living things!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 29634644140032
    m_Localized: "It takes 365 days for Earth to go around the Sun, and that\u2019s
      what we call a year!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 29674401947648
    m_Localized: "Earth has one moon, and it helps create the ocean\u2019s tides
      and lights up the night sky."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 29841364606976
    m_Localized: "Jupiter is the biggest planet in our solar system \u2014 it's so
      big that more than 1,300 Earths could fit inside it!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 29881814474752
    m_Localized: "It has a giant storm called the Great Red Spot that\u2019s been
      spinning for over 300 years \u2014 it\u2019s like a huge hurricane on Jupiter!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 29889427136512
    m_Localized: "Jupiter is made of gas, not solid ground like Earth. You couldn't
      stand on it \u2014 you'd sink into clouds of gas!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 29896217714688
    m_Localized: It has at least 95 moons, and some of them, like Europa and Ganymede,
      might even have oceans under their surfaces.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 29904165920768
    m_Localized: "Jupiter has super strong gravity, much stronger than Earth\u2019s
      \u2014 it's the reason Jupiter can hold on to so many moons and even pull in
      space rocks that could hit Earth."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 30001876426752
    m_Localized: "Mars is called the \"Red Planet\" \u2013 It gets its red color
      from iron in the soil, which has rusted over time!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 30129475543040
    m_Localized: "Mars has the tallest volcano in the solar system! \u2013 Olympus
      Mons is about three times taller than Mount Everest!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 30147020316672
    m_Localized: "A day on Mars is almost like Earth\u2019s! \u2013 One day on Mars
      is 24 hours and 37 minutes, just a little longer than a day on Earth."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 30154662338560
    m_Localized: "Mars has huge dust storms! \u2013 These storms can cover the entire
      planet and last for months!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 30161826209792
    m_Localized: "There might have been water on Mars! \u2013 Scientists believe
      that long ago, Mars had rivers, lakes, and even oceans!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 30263844265984
    m_Localized: "Mercury is the closest planet to the Sun \u2014 it\u2019s the first
      planet in our solar system!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 30664106696704
    m_Localized: "It gets super hot during the day (over 400\xB0C) but freezing cold
      at night \u2014 that\u2019s because it has almost no atmosphere to hold heat."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 30671547392000
    m_Localized: "One day on Mercury is really long \u2014 it takes about 59 Earth
      days for Mercury to spin around once!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 30677864013824
    m_Localized: "Mercury has no moons \u2014 it\u2019s too close to the Sun to hold
      onto any."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 30686089043968
    m_Localized: "Mercury\u2019s surface looks like the Moon \u2014 it\u2019s full
      of craters from space rocks hitting it!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 30786332909568
    m_Localized: "Neptune is the farthest planet from the Sun \u2014 it\u2019s the
      8th planet in our solar system!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 30813990150144
    m_Localized: "It\u2019s super windy \u2014 Neptune has the strongest winds in
      the whole solar system, blowing faster than 1,200 mph (2,000 km/h)!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 30821804138496
    m_Localized: "It\u2019s a gas giant \u2014 made mostly of gases like hydrogen
      and helium, with a deep blue color."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 30844260442112
    m_Localized: "It has a giant storm called the Great Dark Spot, kind of like Jupiter\u2019s
      storm but darker and smaller"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 30853919924224
    m_Localized: "Neptune has 14 moons \u2014 the biggest one is Triton, which spins
      the opposite way of Neptune\u2019s rotation!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 30931950755840
    m_Localized: "Saturn has beautiful rings \u2014 It\u2019s famous for its big,
      bright rings made of ice, rocks, and dust!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 30960690126848
    m_Localized: "It\u2019s a gas giant \u2014 Just like Jupiter, Saturn is mostly
      made of gases and doesn\u2019t have a solid surface to stand on."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 30967719780352
    m_Localized: "Saturn has lots of moons \u2014 It has over 80 moons, and the biggest
      one is Titan, which is even larger than Mercury!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 30974338392064
    m_Localized: "It\u2019s super fast at spinning \u2014 A day on Saturn is only
      about 10.5 hours long because it spins so quickly!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 30975126921216
    m_Localized: "It\u2019s lighter than water \u2014 If there were a big enough
      bathtub, Saturn would float in it because it\u2019s so light for its size!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 31064553676800
    m_Localized: "Uranus is blue-green \u2014 Its pretty color comes from methane
      gas in its atmosphere, which absorbs red light and reflects blue!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 31085902684160
    m_Localized: "It rolls like a ball \u2014 Uranus spins on its side, unlike any
      other planet! It's tilted so much it looks like it's rolling around the Sun"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 31093339185152
    m_Localized: "It\u2019s an ice giant \u2014 Uranus is made mostly of icy materials
      like water, methane, and ammonia, not just gas like Jupiter or Saturn."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 31099894882304
    m_Localized: "It has rings too! \u2014 Uranus has faint rings that are hard to
      see, but they\u2019re real and circle the planet."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 31106689654784
    m_Localized: "It\u2019s one of the coldest planets \u2014 Even though Neptune
      is farther from the Sun, Uranus gets colder, with temperatures dropping to
      \u2013224\xB0C (\u2013371\xB0F)!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 31196628115456
    m_Localized: "Venus is the brightest planet \u2014 It shines so bright in the
      sky that you can often see it just after sunset or before sunrise. That\u2019s
      why it\u2019s called the \u201CEvening Star\u201D or \u201CMorning Star\u201D!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 31238940254208
    m_Localized: "It\u2019s the hottest planet \u2014 Even though Mercury is closer
      to the Sun, Venus is hotter, with surface temperatures over 460\xB0C (860\xB0F)
      \u2014 hot enough to melt lead!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 31249627340800
    m_Localized: "It spins backward \u2014 Venus rotates in the opposite direction
      of most other planets, and it spins very slowly. A day on Venus is longer than
      its year!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 31256040431616
    m_Localized: "It has thick, toxic clouds \u2014 Venus is covered with thick clouds
      of carbon dioxide and sulfuric acid, trapping heat like a super-powered greenhouse"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 31302869835776
    m_Localized: "It\u2019s Earth\u2019s \u201Ctwin\u201D \u2014 Venus is almost
      the same size and made of similar rock as Earth, which is why people call it
      Earth\u2019s \u201Csister planet\u201D \u2014 but it\u2019s way too hot to
      live on!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 113025872756736
    m_Localized: Humus-Rich Earth Clump
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 113242563084288
    m_Localized: "Collected from fertile soil, this sample is full of organic matter
      and microbes that help plants grow. Earth\u2019s soil is alive with billions
      of bacteria and fungi that support ecosystems."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 113263735930880
    m_Localized: Pond Water Microdrop
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 113274116833280
    m_Localized: This tiny vial holds clean water from a small lake, with trace minerals
      and microscopic life like algae and protozoa. It shows how freshwater ecosystems
      support both animals and plants.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 113317142003712
    m_Localized: Clean Atmosphere Sample
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 113329615863808
    m_Localized: "This capsule contains a portion of Earth\u2019s breathable air
      \u2014 78% nitrogen, 21% oxygen, and traces of other gases. It\u2019s a perfectly
      balanced mix for complex life."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 113344132349952
    m_Localized: Leaf Tissue Extract
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 113363572948992
    m_Localized: This slide holds a microscopic view of leaf cells, where photosynthesis
      happens. It shows how plants convert sunlight and carbon dioxide into food
      and oxygen.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 113385928589312
    m_Localized: Basalt Magma Shard
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 113405822173184
    m_Localized: "This shard of cooled lava comes from a volcano. It tells the story
      of Earth\u2019s inner heat and shifting plates, shaping the land we walk on."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 113418472194048
    m_Localized: Microplastic Fiber Cluster
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 113429796814848
    m_Localized: This sample contains tiny plastic fibers left by human activity.
      These particles are now found in water, soil, and even the air, showing how
      human impact reaches everywhere.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 113635292545024
    m_Localized: Striped Atmosphere Extract
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 113675717246976
    m_Localized: "Jupiter\u2019s colorful stripes are made of fast-moving ammonia
      clouds swirling in opposite directions. This sample came from one of those
      windy bands that help create Jupiter\u2019s famous striped look!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 113699075325952
    m_Localized: Storm Core Fragment
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 113709774995456
    m_Localized: "This swirling bit came from the Great Red Spot\u2014a massive storm
      bigger than Earth that\u2019s been spinning on Jupiter for over 300 years!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 113737499344896
    m_Localized: Jovian Thunderbolt Charge
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 113749260173312
    m_Localized: "This charged vial holds a spark from one of Jupiter\u2019s powerful
      lightning storms\u201410 times stronger than Earth\u2019s and flashing deep
      inside the thick clouds!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 113766591037440
    m_Localized: Upper Cloud Ice Crystal
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 113776435068928
    m_Localized: "This frozen flake formed from ammonia in Jupiter\u2019s upper atmosphere,
      where it\u2019s cold enough for chemical snow to fall from the sky!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 113794340552704
    m_Localized: Jupiter Magnetosphere Scanner
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 113811130351616
    m_Localized: "This detector recorded Jupiter\u2019s massive magnetic field\u2014it\u2019s
      stronger than any planet\u2019s and stretches millions of kilometers into space!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 113831808270336
    m_Localized: Hypothetical Core Pressure Cell
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 113843854311424
    m_Localized: This sample simulates the crushing pressure deep inside Jupiter,
      where scientists think a rocky core may be hiding beneath layers of liquid
      and gas!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 113891413524480
    m_Localized: Oxidized Martian Regolith
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 113911978196992
    m_Localized: "This dusty soil is full of iron that has rusted over time. That\u2019s
      why Mars looks red from space! Unlike Earth, this rust covers almost the entire
      surface."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 113937680891904
    m_Localized: Frozen Water Shard
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 113952780386304
    m_Localized: "This icy chip came from Mars\u2019 south pole. Scientists think
      frozen water hides deep underground, and long ago, there may have been rivers
      and lakes flowing across the planet."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 113975303798784
    m_Localized: Thin Air Bubble
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 113992370421760
    m_Localized: "This tiny air bubble shows just how thin the Martian air is. There\u2019s
      barely any oxygen, and spacesuits are a must! Even boiling water acts strangely
      here because of the pressure."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114005959966720
    m_Localized: Solar Radiation Tracer
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114016655441920
    m_Localized: "This sample tracks powerful rays from space. Without a magnetic
      field like Earth\u2019s, Mars gets hit by solar radiation all the time\u2014future
      astronauts need serious protection"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114033873059840
    m_Localized: Stormborne Dust Layer
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114059282153472
    m_Localized: This fine dust came from a storm that stretched across the whole
      planet! Martian storms are huge, and they can block out sunlight for days.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114072833949696
    m_Localized: Olympus Lava Fragment
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114096720510976
    m_Localized: "This rock may have come from Olympus Mons, the biggest volcano
      in the solar system! Even though it\u2019s inactive now, it once erupted with
      powerful lava flows."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114119562690560
    m_Localized: Extreme Temperature Crystal
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114162545917952
    m_Localized: "Collected from Mercury's sun-facing side, this heat-damaged crystal
      survived temperatures over 430\xB0C. It\u2019s warped, partially melted, and
      holds trace energy from intense solar radiation"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114181130878976
    m_Localized: Shadow Ice Fragment
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114195307626496
    m_Localized: "From a crater in permanent shadow near Mercury's poles, this sample
      holds frozen water, preserved in total darkness at -180\xB0C, despite the planet\u2019s
      closeness to the Sun."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114213796118528
    m_Localized: Crater Dust Cluster
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114223300411392
    m_Localized: "This dusty clump is made of fine, grayish soil created by constant
      meteor impacts. Mercury\u2019s surface is covered with regolith\u2014dust and
      crushed rock\u2014with no atmosphere to slow impacts."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114243554705408
    m_Localized: Mercury Magneto Capsule
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114254229209088
    m_Localized: Despite being small, Mercury has a weak but active magnetic field,
      likely generated by a partially molten core. This capsule contains a trace
      of its magnetic activity.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114282402349056
    m_Localized: Impact Spark Shard
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114308574806016
    m_Localized: "With no real atmosphere to protect it, Mercury is constantly bombarded
      by tiny space rocks. This shard came from a fresh crater \u2014 still warm
      when collected."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114330787840000
    m_Localized: Spin-Orbit Beacon
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114384382656512
    m_Localized: "Mercury rotates three times for every two orbits around the Sun
      \u2014 a 3:2 resonance. This device records that strange rhythm, showing how
      Mercury\u2019s slow day is tied to its orbit."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114413012975616
    m_Localized: Supercooled Methane Shard
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114444499615744
    m_Localized: "Neptune\u2019s blue color comes from methane gas in its atmosphere.
      At high altitudes, it gets so cold that methane freezes into tiny crystals,
      making the planet glow deep blue."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114497347846144
    m_Localized: High-Pressure Sky Sample
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114510727675904
    m_Localized: Pressure inside Neptune rises so fast it could crush a spacecraft.
      Just a few hundred kilometers down, the pressure is thousands of times stronger
      than on Earth.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114529866285056
    m_Localized: Supersonic Anemometer
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114538867261440
    m_Localized: "Neptune\u2019s winds blow over 2,000 km/h, the fastest in the solar
      system. These super-fast jet streams are powered by Neptune\u2019s inner heat,
      not sunlight."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114559499042816
    m_Localized: Slushy Mantle Droplet
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114569628286976
    m_Localized: "Beneath Neptune\u2019s clouds might be a slushy ocean made of water,
      ammonia, and methane. It could even be superionic, where water behaves like
      a mix of solid and liquid."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114581166817280
    m_Localized: Diamond Dust Sample
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114614612197376
    m_Localized: "Neptune\u2019s deep interior may turn carbon into falling diamonds.
      Intense pressure crushes carbon atoms into crystals that might rain through
      the planet"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114625479639040
    m_Localized: Magnetic Field Detector
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114649643024384
    m_Localized: "Neptune\u2019s magnetic field is tilted and off-center, spinning
      in a strange way. It\u2019s likely created in a shallow zone, unlike Earth\u2019s
      deep magnetic core."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114681616203776
    m_Localized: Ice-Rock Ring Fragment
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114707205652480
    m_Localized: "This icy chunk was collected from Saturn\u2019s rings, which are
      made of billions of pieces of ice and rock, some as small as grains and others
      as big as mountains. These rings are thin but stretch out over 280,000 km wide!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114725517983744
    m_Localized: Polar Vortex Fragment
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114736934879232
    m_Localized: "This piece comes from Saturn\u2019s bizarre hexagon-shaped storm
      at its north pole. The storm is massive\u2014wider than Earth\u2014and its
      six-sided shape has puzzled scientists for years!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114750671224832
    m_Localized: Saturnian Storm Echo
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114762885038080
    m_Localized: "This capsule captured radio signals from powerful lightning storms
      deep in Saturn\u2019s atmosphere. These \u201CSaturn Electrostatic Discharges\u201D
      can last for days and create more energy than anything on Earth!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114774641672192
    m_Localized: Upper Atmosphere Flake
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114800965124096
    m_Localized: "This crystal formed from supercooled hydrogen in Saturn\u2019s
      upper atmosphere, where winds blow over 1,800 km/h and temperatures can drop
      below -170\xB0C!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114817129971712
    m_Localized: Reflective Particle Residue
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114832997023744
    m_Localized: "This shimmering dust was gathered from the shadowed areas of Saturn\u2019s
      rings. Some particles are darkened by micrometeorites and cosmic radiation,
      which slowly change their composition over time."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114849321254912
    m_Localized: Saturn Magnetosphere Reader
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114865716789248
    m_Localized: "This device recorded Saturn\u2019s powerful and mysterious magnetic
      field. It\u2019s nearly perfectly aligned with the planet\u2019s rotation\u2014a
      rare feature that scientists still don\u2019t fully understand!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114888030486528
    m_Localized: Methane Ice Crystal
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114918112034816
    m_Localized: "This crystal contains frozen methane, the gas that gives Uranus
      its signature blue color. Methane absorbs red light and reflects blue. It\u2019s
      like holding the planet\u2019s glow in your hand!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114936671830016
    m_Localized: Ionized Gas Orb
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114953696509952
    m_Localized: "This glowing sphere is full of charged particles from Uranus\u2019s
      upper atmosphere. It helps explain why the planet has strange magnetic activity\u2014even
      though it spins almost sideways!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114972294053888
    m_Localized: Deep Mantle Fragment
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 114993320099840
    m_Localized: "This rocky shard likely came from deep beneath the clouds. Uranus
      has an icy mantle full of water, ammonia, and silicate rock\u2014this sample
      may have broken loose during a storm or quake."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 115008146964480
    m_Localized: Ammonia Ice Flake
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 115031240802304
    m_Localized: "A fragile layer of frozen ammonia and water ice, this sample came
      from the lower cloud layers of Uranus. It shows how cold and complex the planet\u2019s
      atmosphere really is!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 115068565913600
    m_Localized: Magneto-Core Tracker
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 115079068450816
    m_Localized: "This compact sensor gathered magnetic readings across Uranus\u2019s
      strange field. Scientists use data like this to map how the planet\u2019s magnetosphere
      tilts wildly as it rotates."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 115108659265536
    m_Localized: Atmospheric Temperature Core
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 115122538217472
    m_Localized: "Despite being far from the Sun, Uranus is colder than Neptune!
      This sample confirms Uranus has the coldest atmosphere of all planets, reaching
      \u2013224\xB0C."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 115161373278208
    m_Localized: Sulfuric Mist Droplet
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 115185847042048
    m_Localized: "Collected from Venus\u2019s thick clouds, this droplet contains
      sulfuric acid, the main ingredient in Venus\u2019s toxic atmosphere. The clouds
      are so dense, they reflect most sunlight and trap intense heat."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 115214372503552
    m_Localized: Baked Basalt Slab
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 115228465364992
    m_Localized: "This scorched rock was taken from Venus\u2019s surface, where temperatures
      reach over 460\xB0C \u2014 hotter than Mercury! The rock is cracked and dry
      from volcanic heat and pressure."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 115245313884160
    m_Localized: Venusian Compression Unit
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 115256193908736
    m_Localized: "This sealed device captured the incredible surface pressure on
      Venus, which is 90 times greater than Earth\u2019s \u2014 enough to crush submarines."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 115269263360000
    m_Localized: Static Storm Collector
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 115283830177792
    m_Localized: Venus experiences intense lightning in its thick clouds, possibly
      due to swirling dust and fast-moving winds. This sample glows with trapped
      static energy from the storm.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 115292004876288
    m_Localized: Volcanic Residue Bead
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 115306940792832
    m_Localized: "Venus may still have active volcanoes. This molten bead was gathered
      from a region showing recent lava flows \u2014 evidence that Venus might be
      geologically alive."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 115323470544896
    m_Localized: Unusual Chemical Trace
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 115343754199040
    m_Localized: "This tiny bubble holds a strange chemical compound found in Venus\u2019s
      upper atmosphere. Some scientists wonder if it\u2019s a sign of unknown chemical
      processes, or even microbial life."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 132307871517679616
    m_Localized: Find the Small Plant
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 132308008080023552
    m_Localized: Look for the glowing plant on Earth, near the spaceship.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 132321511604002816
    m_Localized: Analyze the Small Plant
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 132321698187616256
    m_Localized: Bring the Small Plant to the Space Lab
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 132604815740960768
    m_Localized: "Let\u2019s start our Earth mission!\nFind the glowing Small Plant
      near the spaceship."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 132605662713544704
    m_Localized: 'Great job! You found the Small Plant.

      Now bring it to the
      spaceship lab so we can study it.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 132700000000000001
    m_Localized: Find the Water Drop
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 132700000000000002
    m_Localized: Analyze the Water Drop
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 132700000000000003
    m_Localized: Find the Soil Sample
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 132700000000000004
    m_Localized: Analyze the Soil Sample
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 132700000000000101
    m_Localized: 'Excellent! Our next Earth mission is to find a Water Drop sample.

      Look
      near the spaceship and collect it.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 132700000000000102
    m_Localized: Great work! Now bring the Water Drop to the spaceship lab so we
      can study it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 132700000000000103
    m_Localized: 'Now we need a Soil Sample from Earth.

      Find one near the
      spaceship and collect it.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 132700000000000104
    m_Localized: Nice discovery! Bring the Soil Sample to the spaceship lab so we
      can analyze it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 137706533300420608
    m_Localized: Grow Plant
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
